    <div class="triad-modal__content">
      <h2 class="triad-modal__title">The Science Behind Propolis</h2>
      <p class="triad-modal__description">
        In the hive, propolis is the sealant bees use to patch the honeycomb, keep out invaders, and maintain a sterile, stable environment. It's the hive's defense system. Researchers have spent decades asking whether it plays a similar protective role in the human body — and in 2025, one of the largest analyses to date brought the evidence together in one place.
      </p>
      <div class="triad-modal__plate">
        Published in <a href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="triad-modal__study-link">Frontiers in Nutrition</a>, this systematic review and meta-analysis pooled data from 27 randomized controlled trials and nearly 1,540 adult participants, examining propolis's relationship to the body's inflammatory response and antioxidant status — two of the body's core internal-balance systems.
      </div>
      <h3 class="triad-modal__orange-title">What the analysis found:</h3>
      <ul class="triad-modal__list">
        <li class="triad-modal__list-item">
          <svg class="triad-modal__list-icon" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M14.0472 17.6537L19.7012 11.9999L14.0472 6.34619L12.9934 7.43069L16.8127 11.2499H4.29717V12.7499H16.8127L12.9934 16.5692L14.0472 17.6537Z" fill="#D16F55"/>
          </svg>
          <span>Propolis intake was associated with favorable changes across several markers linked to the body's inflammatory response</span>
        </li>
        <li class="triad-modal__list-item">
          <svg class="triad-modal__list-icon" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M14.0472 17.6537L19.7012 11.9999L14.0472 6.34619L12.9934 7.43069L16.8127 11.2499H4.29717V12.7499H16.8127L12.9934 16.5692L14.0472 17.6537Z" fill="#D16F55"/>
          </svg>
          <span>Propolis intake was associated with favorable changes across several markers linked to the body's antioxidant defenses — how well the body neutralizes everyday oxidative stress</span>
        </li>
        <li class="triad-modal__list-item">
          <svg class="triad-modal__list-icon" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M14.0472 17.6537L19.7012 11.9999L14.0472 6.34619L12.9934 7.43069L16.8127 11.2499H4.29717V12.7499H16.8127L12.9934 16.5692L14.0472 17.6537Z" fill="#D16F55"/>
          </svg>
          <span>These patterns held up across a combined pool of more than 1,500 participants, making this one of the largest bodies of evidence assembled on propolis to date</span>
        </li>
        <li class="triad-modal__list-item">
          <svg class="triad-modal__list-icon" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M14.0472 17.6537L19.7012 11.9999L14.0472 6.34619L12.9934 7.43069L16.8127 11.2499H4.29717V12.7499H16.8127L12.9934 16.5692L14.0472 17.6537Z" fill="#D16F55"/>
          </svg>
          <span>No serious safety concerns were identified across the reviewed trials; reported side effects were generally described as infrequent and mild</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="triad-modal__bottom-text">
        This is exactly the internal "shield" concept our formula is built around: supporting the body's own defense and internal-balance systems, not working around them.
      </p>
